v = (l : ℂ) • v) (h_H004 : (∃ (ι : Type) (b : Module.Basis ι ℤ M) (c : Module.Basis ι ℂ V), ∀ i, (b i : V) = c i) ∧ (∀ r : ℕ, (∀ m : M, LR.divided x r m ∈ M) ∧ (∀ m : M, LR.divided y r m ∈ M))), ∃ A : LR.Actions M x y h, Nontrivial (LR.VK K M) ∧ ∀ W : Submodule K (LR.VK K M), LR.inv W (LR.induced K M A.lx.map) → LR.inv W (LR.induced K M A.ly.map) → LR.inv W (LR.induced K M A.lh.map) → W = ⊥ ∨ W = ⊤\",\"correspondence\":{\"mode\":\"equivalent\",\"explanation\":\"l ranges over naturals, identified bijectively with integers λ≥0; l<p is precisely the original bound. V, K, p, generators, highest vector and arbitrary M are universally parameterized. H002 encodes the complex Chevalley representation by its generators, dimension and irreducibility, and H003 supplies its nonzero highest-weight vector. An additive subgroup of V is uniquely an integer submodule, so H004 is exactly a shared integer/complex basis and stability under all divided powers; generator stability is equivalent to stability under their generated integer enveloping algebra. VK is K⊗Z M, identified with M⊗Z K by the canonical flip in both directions. Actions consists of restrictions to M with agreement in V; agreement determines each map uniquely because the inclusion M→V is injective. Existence is proved, not assumed (T014 constructs restrictions using H004 and h=xy-yx). Its induced maps act on pure tensors by k⊗m↦k⊗f(m), corresponding under the flip to m⊗k↦f(m)⊗k. Thus the existential choice of Actions neither weakens invariance nor adds a hypothesis: under H002,H004 restrictions exist and all choices coincide, so either formulation yields the other. Nontrivial is nonzeroness of the vector space, and bottom/top are zero/all subspaces. Invariance under x,y,h is equivalent to invariance under the abstract rank-three Chevalley Lie algebra: invariance under each generator implies invariance under every linear combination, and the reverse follows by specializing to generators. No faithfulness or distinct reduced weights, algebraic closure, p>2 or l>0 is imposed.\"}}},\"library_terms\":{}}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"search_external_sources","description":"Follow source-retrieval.md: arxiv first (default; an exact arXiv ID is allowed), then google title/author search, then google title/author DOI search, then scihub with a confirmed DOI. Use browser:true for normal local-browser readback of JavaScript/verification pages. Results and DOI strings are locators, not source/theorem approval. Record failed access and continue conditionally when the original stays unavailable.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"},"engine":{"type":"string","enum":["arxiv","google","scihub"]},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_external_source","description":"Read and retain a public HTTPS source and its hash-bound access record. Use offset to continue cached text. Retry with browser:true for a normal isolated local Chrome session if HTTPS needs JavaScript or verification. The optional browser uses ordinary site controls; unsupported challenges remain explicit failures. Verify full PDF identity, version, theorem and context yourself.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"url":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"},"browser":{"type":"boolean"}},"required":["url"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read one declared frozen document. For JSON use pointer (empty string lists the root); large objects return keys, and strings resume with offset=next_offset. For text use inclusive start/end lines and column=next_column when continuing a long line. Every serialized result is at most 32 KiB. Follow has_more and the returned continuation coordinates; no arbitrary local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"integer"},"limit":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report an actual obstacle using these five direct fields. Countercheck the alleged implication against the complete definitions, quantifiers and inequality directions; a feasible example alone does not determine an extremum. A fact not yet proved or registered in the current draft is an obligation to complete, not by itself a gap. For a mathematical stop, identify the concrete implication and actual mathematical difficulty encountered during normal checking/completion, not merely unfilled inventory or exposition. No fixed time/attempt count or counterexample is required. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP/SUSPECTED_GAP stop for an actual supported mathematical obstruction; INPUT_CONFLICT stops for incompatible inputs. In NL0, use source retrieval and explicit conditional deferral for unavailable primary texts; MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT requires that no complete secondary statement can be obtained. Other stages may report SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE for an actual access obstacle. Ordinary unfinished work is not an obstacle report. No mathematical acceptance is generated.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"status":{"type":"string","enum":["SUBSTANTIVE_GAP","SUSPECTED_GAP","SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE","MISSING_SOURCE_STATEMENT","INPUT_CONFLICT"]},"location":{"type":"string"},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"basis":{"type":"string"},"partial_progress":{"type":"string"}},"required":["status","location","explanation","basis","partial_progress"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_assembly_feedback","description":"Read only this author stage's saved candidate, generated proof or full native diagnostics. Positive candidate ID; inclusive line bounds. No other case or arbitrary path is accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["mapping","feedback","proof_source","audit_source","assembly_inputs","mechanical","assembly","inspection","compiler_stdout","compiler_stderr","assembly_stdout","assembly_stderr"]},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"},"column":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["candidate","kind","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"8f7225a8-ac3f-414d-b43d-85650ff75810","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34038,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":1792,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":910,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":22},"total_tokens":34948,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_03155c89c72fc7e7016ae2211387a48191b71696991a94e075":{"input_tokens":31,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_03155c89c72fc7e7016ae22116b28c81919cfa07542f74db73":{"input_tokens":36,"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_03155c89c72fc7e7016ae2211c6c548191ba0d18487cad1939":{"input_tokens":37,"cached_t